1
00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:10,590
KineGate: a ticker and a good-looking price are not enough. Bind the issuer, clocks
and exact intention before acting.

2
00:00:10,590 --> 00:00:17,720
Preflight uses FIXTURE data. Evidence includes REPLAY of real API acquisition. No
wallet, signed transaction or broadcast; this is the actual yellow/black product.

3
00:00:17,720 --> 00:00:26,990
One $50 intention. Thirteen deterministic checks cover identity, permission, clocks,
balance, cost, vendor and effects.

4
00:00:26,990 --> 00:00:35,050
The local receipt binds every input using canonical JSON and SHA-256. A hash proves
internal consistency, not issuer authenticity.

5
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:41,630
Local simulation records this bound fixture once per browser session. No chain
transaction is sent.

6
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:50,270
Change the amount to $51: the previous receipt becomes invalid. KineGate does not
invent a new quote.

7
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:58,950
The weekend case waits: stale independent reference plus a closed underlying market.
Closure is policy context, not a universal DEX ban.

8
00:00:58,950 --> 00:01:06,070
Same ticker, different issuer: the exact intended claim does not match. A ticker
cannot substitute for issuer-specific rights.

9
00:01:06,070 --> 00:01:14,790
Restore a valid fixture, then advance the virtual clock 60 seconds: the receipt
expires and dependent evidence must be refreshed.

10
00:01:14,790 --> 00:01:24,380
Same sixteen authored fixtures: a simplified price-only rule accepts thirteen
policy-unsafe cases; KineGate accepts none. This is not a real-world accuracy
estimate.

11
00:01:24,380 --> 00:01:34,160
REPLAY of four authenticated Binance RWA calls: HTTP200 and business code0. Exact
AAPLon issuer and contract agree; absent execution evidence remains WAIT.

12
00:01:34,160 --> 00:01:43,810
A real 6 USDT quote succeeded: LiquidMesh, actual mode SWAP. This is a recorded
quote, with no declared expiry or minimum output and no trade authorization.

13
00:01:43,810 --> 00:01:52,430
The unsigned SWAP builder and actual off-chain simulation returned HTTP200 and code0.
Predicted execution FAILED: token balance insufficient. No signature, approval or
broadcast.

14
00:01:52,430 --> 00:01:59,970
The pinned-block BSC read matches current API-listed AAPLon: code, symbol, eighteen
decimals. Contract existence does not prove liquidity or settlement.

15
00:01:59,970 --> 00:02:06,520
Mainnet settlement remains unverified. Asset signing needs separate human
authorization; the required DevEx report must be personally authored.

16
00:02:06,520 --> 00:02:13,810
Run it without a wallet. Inspect the code, exported receipt, test evidence and
documented limitations. Evidence before action.
